Subject: hwdec_d3d11egl: copy padded decoder surfaces before ANGLE sampling

Copy the visible, even-aligned NV12/P010 region into a reusable GPU texture
when decoder surface dimensions include padding. This keeps GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE
from sampling the decoder padding without introducing a CPU copy-back.

Use the ANGLE device immediate context and flush acquired GL reads before
reusing the copy texture. Track acquisition so failed mappings do not release
an unacquired stream. Unpadded surfaces keep the existing direct path.

Local patch for mpv v0.41.0; inspired by video/out/d3d11/hwdec_d3d11va.c.

